.TH DTME 1 "May 2026" "dtme" "User Commands"
.
.SH NAME
dtme \- distributed television mass encoder
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dtme
.B \-\-source\-dir
.I dir
.B \-\-output\-dir
.I dir
.B \-\-ffmpeg\-flags
.I flags
.RI [ options ]
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dtme
is a parallel, distributed video encoding pipeline built on top of FFmpeg.
It is designed for mass-encoding large libraries of television or other video
content, coordinating multiple worker processes using filesystem-level locking
so that it can safely run across multiple machines sharing a common network
drive simultaneously.
.PP
At startup,
.B dtme
forks into two processes.
The
.I UI process
(the one the shell launched) stays in the foreground, streaming encoding
events to the terminal with
.B [Worker\~N]
prefixes so the user always knows which worker is responsible for which file.
The
.I manager process
(the forked child) calls
.BR setsid (2)
to detach from the controlling terminal, then spawns all worker processes as
its own children and waits for them to finish.
.PP
Workers race to claim files by atomically creating a
.I .lock
file in the output
.I tmp/
directory using
.B O_CREAT|O_EXCL
\(em a syscall that fails if the file already exists.
This guarantees that no two workers \(em whether on the same machine or
different ones \(em will encode the same file at the same time.
.PP
Workers shuffle the file list before each pass, which distributes load more
evenly when running multiple instances across machines.
Once encoding is complete the lock file is deleted and the finished output
is left in
.IR output\-dir /tmp/.
.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-source\-dir " dir"
Directory containing the input video files.
Required.
.TP
.BI \-\-output\-dir " dir"
Directory where encoded files will be written, into a
.I tmp/
subdirectory.
Required.
.TP
.BI \-\-ffmpeg\-flags " flags"
FFmpeg encoding flags as a single quoted string, inserted between the
.B \-i
input path and the output path on every FFmpeg invocation.
Required unless
.B ffmpeg_flags
is set in the configuration file.
.RS
Example:
.I "\-c:v libsvtav1 \-crf 28 \-preset 6 \-c:a libopus \-b:a 192k"
.RE
.TP
.BI \-\-ffmpeg\-binary " path"
Path to the ffmpeg executable.
Useful when ffmpeg is not in
.B PATH
or when a specific build is required (e.g. one with hardware-acceleration support).
Default:
.IR ffmpeg .
Can also be set via
.B ffmpeg_binary
in the configuration file.
.TP
.BI \-\-output\-extension " ext"
Output container extension.
A leading dot is optional;
.I mkv
and
.I .mkv
are both accepted.
Default:
.IR .mkv .
.TP
.BI \-\-input\-extensions " list"
Colon-separated list of file extensions to scan for.
A leading dot is optional for each entry;
.I mkv:mp4:avi
and
.I .mkv:.mp4:.avi
are both accepted.
Defaults to the following formats:
.IR mkv ,
.IR mp4 ,
.IR mov ,
.IR avi ,
.IR webm ,
.IR divx ,
.IR vob ,
.IR evo ,
.IR ogv ,
.IR ogx ,
.IR flv ,
.IR f4v ,
.IR aac ,
.IR flac ,
.IR mp3 ,
.IR ogg ,
.IR opus ,
.IR alac ,
.IR mka ,
.IR pcm ,
.IR aiff ,
.IR wav ,
.IR cda ,
.IR ape .
.TP
.BI \-\-num\-workers " n"
Number of parallel worker processes to spawn.
Default:
.IR 5 .
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-retries " n"
Maximum number of times a worker will retry finding an unlocked file before
signalling all other workers to stop.
Default:
.IR 10 .
.TP
.B \-\-use\-ramdisk
Copy each source file to
.I /tmp
before encoding.
This can improve read throughput when the source resides on a slow or
heavily contended network share.
The temporary copy is removed after encoding completes.
.TP
.B \-\-debug_enable
Write the full FFmpeg command to the worker log file for each encoded file.
.
.SH KEYBOARD CONTROLS
The following keys are recognised while
.B dtme
is running in the foreground and stdin is an interactive terminal.
.TP
.B d
Detach.
The UI process exits, returning the shell prompt immediately.
The manager process and all workers continue running in the background
without interruption.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-C
Abort.
Sends
.B SIGTERM
to the manager's process group, which stops the manager, all workers, and
any
.BR ffmpeg (1)
subprocesses they have running.
.
.SH OUTPUT
Encoded files are written to
.IR output\-dir /tmp/.
Post-processing such as moving files to a final destination or renaming is
left to the user.
.PP
While running in the foreground, events are printed as they occur:
.PP
.RS
.nf
Encoding started (manager PID 12346). Press \(aqd\(aq to detach, Ctrl\-C to abort.
[Worker 0] Started (PID 12347)
[Worker 1] Started (PID 12348)
[Worker 0] Encoding: Show.S01E01.mkv
[Worker 1] Encoding: Show.S01E02.mkv
[Worker 0] Finished: Show.S01E01.mkv
[Worker 0] Encoding: Show.S01E03.mkv
\&...
.fi
.RE
.PP
A
.I .lock
file is present beside the output file for the duration of encoding and is
removed on completion.
A lock file that persists after all
.B dtme
instances have exited indicates an interrupted encode and the file will be
retried on the next run.
.
.SH LOGGING
The manager writes a log named
.BI main_ pid .log
in the working directory from which
.B dtme
was invoked.
Each worker writes its own log to
.IB manager_pid _worker_logs/transcode_ manager_pid _ worker_pid .log
in the same directory.
Worker logs include the full FFmpeg stdout and stderr output for each file.
.PP
If
.B dtme
is detached, the manager log remains the authoritative record of progress.
.
.SH STOPPING
After detaching, the encoding job can be stopped by sending
.B SIGTERM
to the manager's process group:
.PP
.RS
.nf
kill <manager_pid>
.fi
.RE
.PP
Because all workers share the manager's process group (established via
.BR setsid (2)),
a single
.BR kill (1)
is sufficient to terminate the manager, all workers, and any
.BR ffmpeg (1)
child processes.
The manager PID is printed at startup and is also recorded at the top of
.BI main_ pid .log.
.
.SH DISTRIBUTED USE
.B dtme
can be run with identical arguments on multiple machines simultaneously,
as long as all machines have read/write access to the same
.IR \-\-output\-dir .
The
.B O_CREAT|O_EXCL
locking mechanism works correctly across NFS and SMB mounts.
Each machine's workers will independently race to claim unclaimed files;
no coordination beyond a shared filesystem is required.
.
.SH EXAMPLES
Encode a library of TV episodes to AV1 with Opus audio:
.PP
.RS
.nf
dtme \e
  \-\-source\-dir /mnt/nas/shows \e
  \-\-output\-dir /mnt/nas/encoded \e
  \-\-ffmpeg\-flags "\-c:v libsvtav1 \-crf 30 \-preset 5 \-g 240 \e
                   \-c:a libopus \-b:a 128k" \e
  \-\-output\-extension .mkv \e
  \-\-input\-extensions mkv:mp4:avi
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run on two machines simultaneously against a shared NAS:
.PP
.RS
.nf
# Machine A and Machine B \(em same command, started concurrently:
dtme \-\-source\-dir /mnt/nas/shows \-\-output\-dir /mnt/nas/encoded \e
     \-\-ffmpeg\-flags "\-c:v libsvtav1 \-crf 28 \-preset 6 \e
                     \-c:a libopus \-b:a 192k"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Use 8 workers and copy source files to a ramdisk before encoding:
.PP
.RS
.nf
dtme \-\-source\-dir /mnt/nas/shows \-\-output\-dir /mnt/nas/encoded \e
     \-\-ffmpeg\-flags "..." \-\-num\-workers 8 \-\-use\-ramdisk
.fi
.RE
.PP
Detach immediately after starting (unattended batch job):
.PP
.RS
.nf
dtme \-\-source\-dir /data/shows \-\-output\-dir /data/encoded \e
     \-\-ffmpeg\-flags "..." &
# or launch normally and press \(aqd\(aq once workers are confirmed running
.fi
.RE
.
.SH CONFIG FILE
.B dtme
reads
.I ~/.config/dtme.conf
on startup if it exists.
Values in the file become defaults for every run; command-line arguments
always take precedence.
The file uses INI format with a single
.B [defaults]
section.
Boolean values accept
.BR true / false ,
.BR yes / no ,
.BR on / off ,
or
.BR 1 / 0 .
.PP
Available keys:
.TP
.B ffmpeg_binary
Path to the ffmpeg executable.
Equivalent to
.BR \-\-ffmpeg\-binary .
.TP
.B ffmpeg_flags
Default FFmpeg encoding flags.
Setting this makes
.B \-\-ffmpeg\-flags
optional on the command line.
.TP
.B output_extension
Default output container extension.
.TP
.B input_extensions
Default colon-separated list of input extensions to scan for.
.TP
.B num_workers
Default number of parallel worker processes.
.TP
.B max_retries
Default maximum retry count per worker.
.TP
.B use_ramdisk
Set to
.B true
to copy source files to
.I /tmp
before encoding by default.
.TP
.B debug_enable
Set to
.B true
to enable debug logging by default.
.PP
Example configuration:
.PP
.RS
.nf
[defaults]
ffmpeg_binary = /usr/local/bin/ffmpeg
ffmpeg_flags = \-c:v libsvtav1 \-crf 28 \-preset 6 \-c:a libopus \-b:a 192k
output_extension = .mkv
num_workers = 8
use_ramdisk = true
.fi
.RE
.PP
A fully commented example file is distributed as
.I dtme.conf.example
alongside the source.
.
.SH NOTES
Output is always placed in a
.I tmp/
subdirectory of
.IR \-\-output\-dir .
This is intentional: an interrupted encode leaves a partial file in
.I tmp/
rather than in the final destination, making it easy to identify without
accidentally treating it as a completed file.
.PP
If stdin is not a terminal (e.g.\& piped input or a non-interactive
environment), keyboard controls are disabled and the UI process simply
mirrors manager output until encoding is complete or the process is
signalled.
.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR kill (1),
.BR setsid (1),
.BR nfs (5)
